5,1,1,talk,Daisuke,,I think we should look at the incident logs and the time lost to copying records.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,May,,I’m curious about the staffing of the coordination group and how vendor queries are handled.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,I’ll check network coverage at customer plants and in-house developer availability. Those are the usual blind spots.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,"I will examine the capital budget and software allowance, plus the outcomes of the last three internal rollouts.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Kenji,,I want to see the record of cross-unit standardization efforts and how vendor queries are handled.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Daisuke,,I’m a bit nervous about picking the right things. Do you think the incident logs will actually show what goes wrong on the floor?,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, relax. The logs are just data. I’m more worried about who’s actually doing the work behind the scenes.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Daisuke, the logs are just symptoms. I’m checking if the network even works where the app needs to run.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, the logs show symptoms, not causes. I’m checking the budget to see if the money is even there to fix them.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Daisuke, don’t worry. I’m checking the standardization records to see if we’ve made these mistakes before.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Daisuke,,I just want to make sure we aren’t missing the daily reality. The logs feel like the only honest record we have.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, the logs are cold. I care about the warm bodies filling the gaps. Who’s actually writing those notes?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, warm bodies don’t help if the signal drops. I’m verifying if the infrastructure can even support the workload before we assign anyone.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, bodies are irrelevant if the capital line is frozen. I am verifying the recurring allowance to see what is actually affordable before we commit.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Kenji,,"@May, warm bodies are great, but I’m checking if we’ve already tried this. I want to see if the standardization records show a pattern of failure.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Daisuke,,I just want to see the daily losses clearly. The logs are the only honest record we have.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, the logs are just numbers. I’m looking at the people who actually have to absorb the extra work when things go wrong.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
