35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,I found eleven misrouted deliveries and an hour daily lost to copying. It’s not inexperience; it’s just bad data.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, that’s a symptom. I found the coordination group is gutted. Two people are hand-writing every log. That’s a staffing crisis, not a data one.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, staffing is irrelevant if the signal is dead. Half the plants lose coverage afternoons, and device approval took six weeks. The infrastructure is the bottleneck.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, infrastructure is a capital cost. The capital line is frozen. I found the recurring software allowance has room, but only for narrow, single-trade tools that actually survive.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, that matches my findings. Four of six standardization efforts failed because they had no owner. We keep repeating the same mistake.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, the gutted group explains the copying. If we fix the data, maybe they can breathe.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, fixing data won’t hire the missing staff. I found two clerks are drowning in duplicate certificate requests. We need to stop treating people as infinite buffers.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, you’re blaming the people for a broken network. I found the developers are locked in until Q3, and the interfaces are undocumented. We can’t build on sand.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, the frozen capital line confirms your infrastructure concerns are unaffordable. I found the recurring allowance only supports narrow tools that survive, unlike broad systems that get dropped.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@May, the duplicate certificate requests prove the data is fragmented. We need a single source of truth to stop that waste.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Kenji, a single source of truth would stop the copying. But will anyone actually maintain it?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"@Kenji, a single source of truth is great, but who maintains it? I found the coordination group is gutted. Two people are hand-writing every log.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, you’re ignoring the physical reality. Half the sites have no signal, and our devs are locked until Q3. You can’t maintain a hub on a dead network.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, the capital freeze makes your infrastructure concerns unaffordable. The recurring allowance only supports narrow tools that survive, unlike broad systems that get dropped.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Daisuke, that’s the key. Four failed because they had no owner. We need a tool with a clear, single maintainer, not another abandoned project.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Kenji, I agree. If we don’t assign a clear owner, we’ll just lose it again. The daily losses are real, but they need someone to fix them.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,"@Kenji, a clear owner is useless if the roster is empty. I found the coordination group is gutted. Who is actually going to maintain this without breaking the rota?","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, you’re ignoring the physical reality. Half the sites have no signal, and our devs are locked until Q3. You can’t maintain a hub on a dead network.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, the recurring allowance covers narrow tools, not broad systems. The last three broad rollouts were dropped because they demanded daily entry from everyone.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@May, the tool room walkthroughs survived because they were simple and owned. We need that same narrow focus, not a massive system that breaks the rota.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
